ion. Riyadh province.","","text","",""],["World distribution. Asia: IN and TR and newly recorded from SA. Europe: GR (Kovar 2007).","","text","",""]]},"STLYD":{"d":[["Rio de Janeiro","8920","mrgid","native",""]]},"SWYM":{"d":[["","WS","iso","",""]]},"T3PQH":{"d":[["Distribution. NE India (type locality Assam).","","text","",""]]},"T78M":{"d":[["","ITA-IT","tdwg","native",""],["","YUG-SL","tdwg","native",""],["Italy, Slovenia","","text","native",""]]},"TMKD":{"d":[["S-Brazil (Rio Grande do Sul); Uruguay (Canelones, Cerro Largo, Colonia, Florida Prov., Lavalleja, Maldonado, Montevideo, Paysandu, Rio Negro, Rocha, San Jose, Soriano, Treinta y Tres); Argentina (Buenos Aires, Corrientes, Argentina Distrito Federal, Entre Rios, Misiones)","","text","",""]]},"TQCH":{"d":[["peninsular Malaysia (Semangkok Pass, Selangor)","","text","",""]]},"TW786":{"d":[["Distribution. Hong Kong.","","text","",""]]},"TYGPL":{"d":[["Distribution. China (Taiwan). Notes. Helcon albus Chou et Hsu from Taiwan is included in Wroughtonia, because it has a wide obtuse ventral protuberance on the hind femur, the hind tarsus is pale and the antenna has a white band. The species is included provisionally in the key on basis of the original description, because the holotype (and only known specimen of W. alba) was not available for examination. Spasskia anastasiae Belokobylskij from Far East Russia is included in Wroughtonia (as other Spasskia spp.) but is not close to the other species because of the obtuse ventral protuberance of the hind femur and the shape of the first tergite and of the occipital carina. In the key it will come near W. alba because the hind coxa are densely sculptured (transversely rugulose to rugose) dorsally; differs from W. alba by the complete dark brown or black antenna (with white band in W. alba), palpi dark brown basally (brownish yellow), temple and vertex densely and coarsely punctate-rugose (smooth) and hind coxa dark brown or black (brownish yellow).","","text","",""]]